          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.119,
            0.884,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": "Try to get the eyes as symmetrical and identical as possible. This might need many trials."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.177,
            0.582,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": "**B)** (From Construct above (page no. 211)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.206,
            0.884,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": "For the purpose of construction, let us take the side lengths to be of 5 cm. Consider this figure."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.398,
            0.244,
            0.651,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_29_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.414,
            0.884,
            0.481
          ],
          "content": "We need to identify only one more point to make this a 4-sided figure. That point, let us call it D, should be 5 cm from both B and C. How can such a point be found?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.482,
            0.786,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "Can any of the ideas used in the ‘House’ problem be used here?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.424,
            0.539,
            0.63,
            0.565
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Summary"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.585,
            0.884,
            0.628
          ],
          "content": "All the points of a circle are at the same distance from its **centre**. This distance is called the **radius** of the circle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.631,
            0.779,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": "■ A compass can be used to construct circles and their parts."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.654,
            0.884,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": "■ A rough diagram can be useful in planning how to construct a given figure."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.699,
            0.885,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": "■ A rectangle can be constructed given the lengths of its sides or that of one of its sides and a diagonal."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.082,
